        "blob_url": "https://github.com/Gutsken/Autoclip/blob/5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb/README.md",
        "raw_url": "https://github.com/Gutsken/Autoclip/raw/5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb/README.md",
        "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Gutsken/Autoclip/contents/README.md?ref=5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb",
        "patch": "@@ -106,6 +106,20 @@ ollama pull llama3.1:8b\n \n Clip quality tracks model quality closely. A 7B model returns valid JSON full of mediocre picks; a frontier model is noticeably better at spotting a real hook. That's the honest trade for running offline.\n \n+### Optional extras\n+\n+```bash\n+uv pip install -e \".[gpu]\"\n+```\n+\n+CUDA runtime libraries for NVIDIA GPUs. Install these if `doctor` reports that CTranslate2 can't see your GPU \u2014 pip puts them somewhere the OS loader doesn't search, and AutoClip registers the location itself. On macOS this deliberately installs nothing: there's no CUDA there, and Apple Silicon takes the CPU path.\n+\n+```bash\n+uv pip install -e \".[diarization]\"\n+```\n+\n+Speaker diarization via WhisperX \u2014 what lets the reframe stage cut to whoever is talking in a multi-person video. Pulls PyTorch (large), and needs a HuggingFace token plus acceptance of the gated pyannote model licences.\n+\n ### Docker\n \n The guaranteed path \u2014 ffmpeg, Python version, and fonts all pinned:"
      },
      {
        "sha": "5192d240e6f375a298bd21cfa5daa5d35057869f",
        "filename": "pyproject.toml",
        "status": "modified",
        "additions": 7,
        "deletions": 2,
        "changes": 9,
        "blob_url": "https://github.com/Gutsken/Autoclip/blob/5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb/pyproject.toml",
        "raw_url": "https://github.com/Gutsken/Autoclip/raw/5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb/pyproject.toml",
        "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Gutsken/Autoclip/contents/pyproject.toml?ref=5d0eac36fa615b79dd2104083bf273a96f8d68bb",
        "patch": "@@ -69,9 +69,14 @@ diarization = [\n # NVIDIA CUDA 12 runtime libraries for faster-whisper/CTranslate2 on Windows and\n # Linux. Without these the usual failure is a missing cudnn_ops64_9.dll at the\n # first GPU transcribe.\n+# Markers matter here: these wheels are not published for macOS, so without\n+# them `pip install autoclip[gpu]` fails to resolve on a Mac \u2014 which is exactly\n+# what doctor tells you to run when it can't see your GPU. On macOS the extra\n+# now installs nothing, which is correct: there is no CUDA there, and Apple\n+# Silicon takes the CPU path anyway.\n gpu = [\n-  \"nvidia-cublas-cu12>=12.4\",\n-  \"nvidia-cudnn-cu12>=9.1\",\n+  \"nvidia-cublas-cu12>=12.4; platform_system != 'Darwin'\",\n+  \"nvidia-cudnn-cu12>=9.1; platform_system != 'Darwin'\",\n ]\n dev = [\n   \"pytest>=8.3\","
      }
    ]
